# Check every text file out with LF, on every platform.
#
# Without this, a Windows checkout converts these to CRLF, a build there writes
# LF, and `app/index.html` looks changed on every single line — which is what
# the "committed app must match the sources" check in CI first caught. It also
# means the built file is identical whoever builds it, which is the only thing
# that makes that check meaningful.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, and must never be touched by line-ending conversion. The fonts are
# already detected as binary by content, but saying so costs nothing and a
# silently corrupted woff2 is a miserable thing to debug.
*.woff2 binary
*.png   binary
*.ico   binary
*.exe   binary
*.7z    binary

# Generated. Big, one-line-ish, and reviewing its diff is never useful — the
# change to look at is in src/.
app/index.html linguist-generated=true -diff
